      "side": 1,
      "message": "ah, thats my newly discovered trick. for zero it does nothing, for non-zero small positive numbers it increase number of non-zero bits, while for small negative numbers this unsigned multiplication make result further away from -1, so skipping instructions would prevent from getting \u0027b\u0027 with non-zero input. The problem is that in used cases test value can be easily in range 0xfffffff0 - 0xffffffff, so skipping comparison (movne in second variant https://godbolt.org/z/e6Wef96z6 and few other instructions) may result in good enough mask to get \u0027a\u0027:\n\n                              ; r0  \u003d test; r1 \u003d a, r2 \u003d b\n        adds    r3, r0, #0    ; r3 \u003d test\n                              ; test \u003d\u003d 0        test !\u003d 0\n        movne   r3, #1        ; r3 \u003d test \u003d\u003d 0   r3 \u003d 1\n        rsb     r0, r3, #0    ; r0 \u003d 0 - r3 \u003d 0  r0 \u003d -1\n        sub     r3, r3, #1    ; r3 \u003d -1          r3 \u003d -2 (!!)\n        and     r0, r0, r1    ; r0 \u003d 0           r0 \u003d -1 \u0026 a  \u003da\n        and     r3, r3, r2    ; r3 \u003d -1 \u0026 b \u003d b\n        orr     r0, r0, r3    ; choose a or b\nproblem here is r3 is very close all bits set, and skipping movne with test\u003d0xffffffff  makes it very dangerous. After writing this I came up with a simpler approach using value_barrier() :)",
